course: dictionary
lesson: 16181
title: Yelping
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A yelp is a short, sharp, high cry. Dogs and puppies yelp when they are hurt, scared or excited. «The puppy was yelping after it stepped on a sharp stick.» The clue is the sharp stick: something hurt the puppy, so yelping means it is crying out in pain.
explain: People can yelp too. «Ella yelped when the cold water splashed on her toes.» A yelp is quick and sudden, so it is shorter than a long cry or a song.
explain: The same word can show different feelings. «The children ran onto the beach, yelping with joy.» Here yelping shows excitement, not pain. Read the rest of the sentence to find out which feeling it is.
explain: Yelping often tells us that an animal needs care. If you hear a yelping puppy, stay calm, move slowly and check that it is safe. Handle pets gently, because a yelp is a way of saying, «Something is wrong.»
fact: Yelping means making short, sharp, high cries.
fact: Dogs and puppies yelp when they are hurt, scared or excited.
fact: A person can yelp too, with a short cry of pain or surprise.
fact: «Yelping in pain» means crying out sharply because something hurts.
fact: «Yelping with joy» means making short, happy cries when you are excited.
exercise: «The puppy was yelping after it stepped on a sharp stick.» What is the puppy doing? | Sleeping quietly in its basket | Wagging its tail slowly | *Making short, sharp cries of pain | Chewing a soft toy
exercise: «The dog kept yelping at the door until someone came.» Why might the dog be yelping? | It is painting a picture | It is counting the stairs | *It is hurt, scared or wants attention | It is asleep and dreaming happily
exercise: «Yelping with joy, the children ran onto the beach.» How do the children feel? | *Excited and happy | Angry and cross | Bored and sleepy | Hungry and tired
test: «The little puppy was yelping in the rain, so Mia carried it inside.» Why was the puppy yelping? | *It was cold or hurt, so it cried out | It wanted to go swimming | It was hungry for its dinner | It was singing a happy song
test: Which phrase shows a child making a sharp cry of pain? | Singing softly | *Yelping in pain | Smiling quietly | Yawning in bed
exam: Ben heard a yelping sound from the hedge. What should he do first? | Walk away and forget about it | *Check carefully, because something may be hurt and frightened | Shout at the hedge to scare it | Throw a ball into the hedge
